{"kind":"artifact","text":"The documentation of the promise rule at docs, for the same head. Four pages carried the old rule as normative prose and now carry the adopted one: concepts/record.md on what body.to means and on which signer tests the fold actually applies; reference/gs/state.md and reference/mcp/state.md on the request body field and the required edges, including that several actors may promise one request and each promise is its own commitment; how-to/run-a-work-loop.md on addressing as routing rather than reservation, and on what volunteering does not confer.","body":{"commit":"4a72921c9c2f9626cd627bc23adfef8f32fcd113","path":"docs"}}